y externalized source ID>\nSOURCE_VERSION: <exact 64-hex version>\nEVIDENCE_RESULT: <exact newly externalized RESULT ID>\nEVIDENCE_ANCHOR: <one exact unique single-line substring copied from that source inside the delivered result>\nMODE: source_reported_fact or source_reported_relationship\nATTRIBUTION: owner_source_reported\nREFERENTS: NONE or comma-separated exact source IDs named by both the statement and the anchor's containing source line\nAUTHORITY: non_authoritative_derivative\nSTATEMENT: <one complete single-line source-attributed fact or relationship>\n\nThe host, not you, resolves the exact anchor, derives its containing complete source line, byte offsets, hashes, source/version binding, and reopen path. Copy only the smallest exact substring that supports the statement. The containing line preserves adjacent context and qualifications. Each claim is admitted independently; rejected claims consume cost and are discarded without repair or retry. A zero-valid update leaves prior state unchanged and ordinary task work continues.\n\nEmit at most 4 claims per source and 8 total, <= 1500 tokenizer tokens overall and <= 650 per source. A fact cannot name an external source. A relationship may name external objects when the owner-source context names them, but cannot mutate their slots or assert their authoritative current state. Cross-source synthesis belongs in exact task work, not this register.\n\nNEW SOURCE VERSIONS\nCIPHER: 6db7f6a91d666ab9e013e147aa946885080f48117bd461c8a542171378aba4cb\nDELTA: 4c3707d0d2ae07ceb2bda6d83cf6585510f5398db7c66568ba38aa3fd3f01169\n\nPRIOR CURRENT RECORDS FOR THESE SOURCES\n# Anchored provenance-local source register\n\nEMPTY\n\n\nAUTHORITATIVE TASK (relevance only; never evidence)\n# Authoritative task — Solace regional-water recovery decision\n\nSolace County must restore a regional drinking-water network after wildfire,\npower, treatment, hydraulic, and control-system disturbances. Build and maintain\nthe exact candidate files, then propose submission only when the package is\ngenuinely ready for independent review.\n\nThe world contains fourteen exact, versioned source objects with opaque IDs.\nCatalog titles help navigation but do not supply findings. Read the bytes needed\nfor the work and cite sources as `[SOURCE_ID]`.\n\n## Required exact work\n\nMaintain `EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md` as a compact task-native evidence and\ndecision matrix. Preserve source-bound facts, cross-source dependencies,\nconflicts, unknowns, candidate currency, and citations. This exact artifact is\nnon-authoritative but may carry cumulative work across context turnover.\n\nConstruct `BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md` as a 1,500–2,100-word Solace\nWater Recovery Decision with exactly the declared section headings. Use at\nleast eleven distinct source IDs and integrate—not merely list—the governing\nrelationships.\n\nAddress all twelve requirement groups:\n\n- Q01 — incident, utility, public-health, communication, and closure authority;\n- Q02 — pressure, storage, isolation, residence time, and candidate-bound hydraulics;\n- Q03 — sampling rounds, spacing, detection limits, action thresholds, and staleness;\n- Q04 — pump capacity, shared-main limits, staged demand, and current evidence;\n- Q05 — grid, generator, fuel, staffing, chemicals, and resource contingencies;\n- Q06 — treatment barriers, turbidity, disinfectant, source blend, and contact time;\n- Q07 — contamination hypotheses, observations, locations, investigation holds, and falsifiers;\n- Q08 — access, token and key state, immutable custody, retention, and automation restoration;\n- Q09 — telemetry coverage, warnings versus actions, delays, alternates, and uncertainty;\n- Q10 — environmental determination, notice clock, permits, discharge, and evidence custody;\n- Q11 — public advisories, accessibility, alternate water, service states, and communications;\n- Q12 — candidate lineage, rollback, effect uptake, current checks, blockers, independent readiness, and closure.\n\n## Relationship rules\n\nPreserve psi versus kPa, gallons versus treated reserve, micrograms versus\nmilligrams, reporting limits versus action thresholds, percentages versus\nmeasured concentration, rated versus usable power, nameplate versus shared\ncapacity, warnings versus isolation triggers, forecast versus observation, and\nmechanical checks versus public-health and independent readiness. Candidate,\nhydraulic, sampling, treatment, pump, power, key, role, telemetry, or source-\nwater changes can make earlier evidence stale.\n\nThe decision must state owners, inputs, resources, timing, dependencies,\neffects, observations, contingencies, rollback and retirement conditions, and\nevidence that would falsify important claims. Do not infer that a provenance\nrecord, mutation, green check, or submission establishes readiness.\n\n\nEXACT NEWLY EXTERNALIZED RESULTS\n--- NEWLY EXTERNALIZED RESULT-002 ---\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:CIPHER:1-64+DELTA:1-64\",\"object_version\":\"64721c48b86decba9adecca404e0e207db15cc1c0611470f2fe6e28207610bef\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-002\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"CIPHER\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"DELTA\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":8452}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"CIPHER\",\"source_path\":\"sources/CIPHER_LAB.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"6db7f6a91d666ab9e013e147aa946885080f48117bd461c8a542171378aba4cb\",\"source_size_bytes\":3991,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Laboratory sampling, detection limits, and clearance evidence\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe current confirmatory set has zero E. coli positives across forty-eight samples. Clearance requires two complete rounds at least sixteen hours apart; one clean round is insufficient.\nThe benzene reporting limit is 0.5 micrograms per liter and the action threshold is 5.0 micrograms per liter. The reporting limit is not the action threshold and neither is a percent concentration.\nA flow-path, disinfectant-dose, source-water, sampling-plan, or laboratory-method change makes prior samples stale for the changed candidate.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nCIPHER sample placement consumes BASTION flow paths and GARNET contamination hypotheses. HELIX governs chain of custody and laboratory access.\nAURORA consumes current CIPHER findings for advisory decisions; CIPHER does not itself authorize public restoration.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| LAB-000 | entry-point | v2 | 0.0 | positive-samples | superseded |\n| LAB-001 | north-grid | v2 | 1.3 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-002 | south-grid | v2 | 2.6 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-003 | hospital-loop | v2 | 0.8 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-004 | entry-point | v2 | 2.1 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-005 | north-grid | v2 | 0.3 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-006 | south-grid | v2 | 1.6 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-007 | hospital-loop | v2 | 2.9 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-008 | entry-point | v2 | 1.1 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-009 | north-grid | v2 | 2.4 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-010 | south-grid | v2 | 0.6 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-011 | hospital-loop | v2 | 1.9 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-012 | entry-point | v2 | 0.1 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-013 | north-grid | v2 | 1.4 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-014 | south-grid | v3 | 2.7 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-015 | hospital-loop | v3 | 0.9 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-016 | entry-point | v3 | 2.2 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-017 | north-grid | v3 | 0.4 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-018 | south-grid | v3 | 1.7 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-019 | hospital-loop | v3 | 3.0 | positive-samples | superseded |\n| LAB-020 | entry-point | v3 | 1.2 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-021 | north-grid | v3 | 2.5 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-022 | south-grid | v3 | 0.7 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-023 | hospital-loop | v3 | 2.0 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-024 | entry-point | v3 | 0.2 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-025 | north-grid | v3 | 1.5 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-026 | south-grid | v3 | 2.8 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-027 | hospital-loop | v3 | 1.0 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-028 | entry-point | v4 | 2.3 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-029 | north-grid | v4 | 0.5 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-030 | south-grid | v4 | 1.8 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-031 | hospital-loop | v4 | 0.0 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-032 | entry-point | v4 | 1.3 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-033 | north-grid | v4 | 2.6 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-034 | south-grid | v4 | 0.8 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-035 | hospital-loop | v4 | 2.1 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-036 | entry-point | v4 | 0.3 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-037 | north-grid | v4 | 1.6 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-038 | south-grid | v4 | 2.9 | positive-samples | superseded |\n| LAB-039 | hospital-loop | v4 | 1.1 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-040 | entry-point | v4 | 2.4 | positive-samples | current |\n| LAB-041 | north-grid | v4 | 0.6 | positive-samples | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nPreserve rounds, spacing, sample count, detection limit, action threshold, and staleness.\nState what negative result would falsify clearance and trigger renewed isolation.\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"DELTA\",\"source_path\":\"sources/DELTA_PUMPS.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"4c3707d0d2ae07ceb2bda6d83cf6585510f5398db7c66568ba38aa3fd3f01169\",\"source_size_bytes\":4013,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Pump capacity, sequencing, and cavitation constraints\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe treatment works can supply 18 million gallons per day, but the shared transmission main is capped at 14.5 MGD. Pump nameplate capacities cannot be summed into usable system flow.\nThe latest inspected configuration sustained 12.8 MGD after fire-flow and hospital reserve. A higher stage requires a current candidate-bound pump and pressure test.\nRestoration may advance through 10, 30, 60, and 100 percent demand stages only after two thirty-minute windows meet pressure, turbidity, power, and storage gates.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nBASTION supplies pressure limits, ECHO supplies feeder headroom, and FALCON supplies treatment output. All three constrain DELTA sequencing.\nA pump, valve, main allocation, generator, or treatment-train change makes prior capacity evidence stale.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| PMP-000 | pump-1 | v2 | 18.0 | million-gallons-day | superseded |\n| PMP-001 | pump-2 | v2 | 19.3 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-002 | booster-east | v2 | 20.6 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-003 | booster-west | v2 | 18.8 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-004 | pump-1 | v2 | 20.1 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-005 | pump-2 | v2 | 18.3 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-006 | booster-east | v2 | 19.6 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-007 | booster-west | v2 | 20.9 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-008 | pump-1 | v2 | 19.1 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-009 | pump-2 | v2 | 20.4 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-010 | booster-east | v2 | 18.6 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-011 | booster-west | v2 | 19.9 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-012 | pump-1 | v2 | 18.1 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-013 | pump-2 | v2 | 19.4 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-014 | booster-east | v3 | 20.7 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-015 | booster-west | v3 | 18.9 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-016 | pump-1 | v3 | 20.2 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-017 | pump-2 | v3 | 18.4 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-018 | booster-east | v3 | 19.7 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-019 | booster-west | v3 | 21.0 | million-gallons-day | superseded |\n| PMP-020 | pump-1 | v3 | 19.2 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-021 | pump-2 | v3 | 20.5 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-022 | booster-east | v3 | 18.7 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-023 | booster-west | v3 | 20.0 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-024 | pump-1 | v3 | 18.2 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-025 | pump-2 | v3 | 19.5 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-026 | booster-east | v3 | 20.8 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-027 | booster-west | v3 | 19.0 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-028 | pump-1 | v4 | 20.3 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-029 | pump-2 | v4 | 18.5 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-030 | booster-east | v4 | 19.8 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-031 | booster-west | v4 | 18.0 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-032 | pump-1 | v4 | 19.3 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-033 | pump-2 | v4 | 20.6 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-034 | booster-east | v4 | 18.8 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-035 | booster-west | v4 | 20.1 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-036 | pump-1 | v4 | 18.3 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-037 | pump-2 | v4 | 19.6 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-038 | booster-east | v4 | 20.9 | million-gallons-day | superseded |\n| PMP-039 | booster-west | v4 | 19.1 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-040 | pump-1 | v4 | 20.4 | million-gallons-day | current |\n| PMP-041 | pump-2 | v4 | 18.6 | million-gallons-day | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nPreserve shared capacity, observed