a97c476cc4bf7d35c0ba7c807924abd1db10670a20d31f8fb33ac4d61c08\nMODE: source_reported_relationship\nATTRIBUTION: owner_source_reported\nREFERENTS: BASTION,GARNET\nAUTHORITY: non_authoritative_derivative\nSTATEMENT: CIPHER sample placement operationally consumes BASTION flow paths and GARNET contamination hypotheses.\n\n## CLAIM ECHO-GENERATOR-FUEL-DURATION\nSLOT_SOURCE: ECHO\nSOURCE_VERSION: a3826feabfb2389ef861bba819d3ae178c9e9086a8f309722ba1413591ff8395\nEVIDENCE_RESULT: RESULT-003\nEVIDENCE_ANCHOR: Emergency generation can carry 4.1 MW for thirty-six hours at the current fuel stock. The duration is not thirty-six days and excludes mobile-pump load.\nANCHOR_BYTES: 211-363\nANCHOR_SHA256: c99dd93d1fb6f2ffa1c5e581224d94207cb6b2fa4252d2d6e091b71565f53482\nCONTEXT_LINES: 6-6\nCONTEXT_SHA256: dae75ecffd9b89ff430f032d277db11ab848dbff8f5e09475c759c72ec601d77\nMODE: source_reported_fact\nATTRIBUTION: owner_source_reported\nREFERENTS: NONE\nAUTHORITY: non_authoritative_derivative\nSTATEMENT: ECHO reports that emergency generation can carry 4.1 MW for thirty-six hours at the current fuel stock, excluding mobile-pump load.\n\n## CLAIM ECHO-GRID-RATED-VERSUS-USABLE\nSLOT_SOURCE: ECHO\nSOURCE_VERSION: a3826feabfb2389ef861bba819d3ae178c9e9086a8f309722ba1413591ff8395\nEVIDENCE_RESULT: RESULT-003\nEVIDENCE_ANCHOR: The grid feed is rated at 8.2 MW, but the damaged switchgear limits current delivery to 6.5 MW.\nANCHOR_BYTES: 60-155\nANCHOR_SHA256: e8a9e473759bb86edf1bf1589d16762106401c1514dbc274e36451e17f0bb5c4\nCONTEXT_LINES: 5-5\nCONTEXT_SHA256: e03b39ac79855f7322a5a55cc8a77795b652c818e5861d6790a92e538dd7f6e0\nMODE: source_reported_fact\nATTRIBUTION: owner_source_reported\nREFERENTS: NONE\nAUTHORITY: non_authoritative_derivative\nSTATEMENT: ECHO reports that the grid feed is rated at 8.2 MW, but the damaged switchgear limits current delivery to 6.5 MW.\n\n## CLAIM FALCON-CHLORINE-ENTRY-DISTRIBUTION\nSLOT_SOURCE: FALCON\nSOURCE_VERSION: 62997706c361243e5d2720ccc088b53d3bcc2c64e64e6ee054d588aeac8fd8b8\nEVIDENCE_RESULT: RESULT-003\nEVIDENCE_ANCHOR: Free chlorine must remain between 0.8 and 2.0 milligrams per liter at entry points and at least 0.2 mg/L in distribution. Entry and distribution thresholds are different controls.\nANCHOR_BYTES: 221-400\nANCHOR_SHA256: 492fd6157567799723684d1b5630e0c9a44f82e30610f81f020562cf8551f54b\nCONTEXT_LINES: 6-6\nCONTEXT_SHA256: 5583311f69ee21752ce3e3154d8f431500cd2eea3b9343923c2bc389a8e78efe\nMODE: source_reported_fact\nATTRIBUTION: owner_source_reported\nREFERENTS: NONE\nAUTHORITY: non_authoritative_derivative\nSTATEMENT: FALCON reports that free chlorine must remain between 0.8 and 2.0 milligrams per liter at entry points and at least 0.2 mg/L in distribution, noting these are different controls.\n\n## CLAIM FALCON-TURBIDITY-CURRENT-VERSUS-GATE\nSLOT_SOURCE: FALCON\nSOURCE_VERSION: 62997706c361243e5d2720ccc088b53d3bcc2c64e64e6ee054d588aeac8fd8b8\nEVIDENCE_RESULT: RESULT-003\nEVIDENCE_ANCHOR: Current combined-filter turbidity is 0.18 NTU. The release gate is at or below 0.30 NTU for four hours; 0.18 NTU is not a chlorine residual.\nANCHOR_BYTES: 80-220\nANCHOR_SHA256: 3c689b0f45ba4a0ce22a0bef18fa3840cd127123c14f243b788107222b0954d0\nCONTEXT_LINES: 5-5\nCONTEXT_SHA256: ac14208e812cffe870672716e2cd7acf38bab401f3358844a50db82a4c1dd60e\nMODE: source_reported_fact\nATTRIBUTION: owner_source_reported\nREFERENTS: NONE\nAUTHORITY: non_authoritative_derivative\nSTATEMENT: FALCON reports that current combined-filter turbidity is 0.18 NTU, with a release gate at or below 0.30 NTU for four hours, and clarifies that 0.18 NTU is not a chlorine residual.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"read_batch\",\"requests\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"MOSAIC\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"NEXUS\",\"start_line\":1}]\n}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:MOSAIC:1-64+NEXUS:1-64\",\"object_version\":\"ce0798821f875aeea4f1794555e0c92c53cc571a95cfecafa85dbd7dfc319fc1\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-007\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"MOSAIC\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"NEXUS\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":8078}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"MOSAIC\",\"source_path\":\"sources/MOSAIC_CHANGE.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"a3836321537dc4f3ee3cacc094761d5176c0a7f08ae891f4fc4e1ee5b3f84b4d\",\"source_size_bytes\":3861,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Candidate lineage, rollback, and configuration control\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe current recovery candidate is W7 with hydraulic model H12, pump plan P9, treatment plan T6, and key set W4. Evidence for W6 is historical unless explicitly transferred and rechecked.\nRollback to W6 is mechanically possible only while valve map V8 and controller firmware C11 remain compatible. Mechanical possibility is not authorization.\nEvery mutation must record before and after candidate hashes, changed files, affected evidence, check currency, owner, and rollback effect.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nBASTION, CIPHER, DELTA, ECHO, FALCON, and HELIX observations can become stale after MOSAIC candidate changes.\nNEXUS reviews current-candidate evidence independently; AURORA authorizes execution and closure separately.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| CHG-000 | hydraulic-model | v2 | 7.0 | candidate-index | superseded |\n| CHG-001 | pump-plan | v2 | 8.3 | candidate-index | current |\n| CHG-002 | treatment-plan | v2 | 9.6 | candidate-index | current |\n| CHG-003 | key-set | v2 | 7.8 | candidate-index | current |\n| CHG-004 | hydraulic-model | v2 | 9.1 | candidate-index | current |\n| CHG-005 | pump-plan | v2 | 7.3 | candidate-index | current |\n| CHG-006 | treatment-plan | v2 | 8.6 | candi