pendent review of residual risk, and explicit acceptance by the authorized owner.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nNEXUS consumes evidence from AURORA, BASTION, CIPHER, ECHO, FALCON, HELIX, INDIGO, LUMEN, and MOSAIC but does not mutate their states.\nAn artifact, semantic register, mechanical check, or submission proposal cannot self-authorize readiness.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| RDY-000 | hydraulic | v2 | 16.0 | open-findings | superseded |\n| RDY-001 | quality | v2 | 17.3 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-002 | power | v2 | 18.6 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-003 | public-health | v2 | 16.8 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-004 | hydraulic | v2 | 18.1 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-005 | quality | v2 | 16.3 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-006 | power | v2 | 17.6 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-007 | public-health | v2 | 18.9 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-008 | hydraulic | v2 | 17.1 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-009 | quality | v2 | 18.4 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-010 | power | v2 | 16.6 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-011 | public-health | v2 | 17.9 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-012 | hydraulic | v2 | 16.1 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-013 | quality | v2 | 17.4 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-014 | power | v3 | 18.7 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-015 | public-health | v3 | 16.9 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-016 | hydraulic | v3 | 18.2 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-017 | quality | v3 | 16.4 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-018 | power | v3 | 17.7 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-019 | public-health | v3 | 19.0 | open-findings | superseded |\n| RDY-020 | hydraulic | v3 | 17.2 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-021 | quality | v3 | 18.5 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-022 | power | v3 | 16.7 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-023 | public-health | v3 | 18.0 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-024 | hydraulic | v3 | 16.2 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-025 | quality | v3 | 17.5 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-026 | power | v3 | 18.8 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-027 | public-health | v3 | 17.0 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-028 | hydraulic | v4 | 18.3 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-029 | quality | v4 | 16.5 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-030 | power | v4 | 17.8 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-031 | public-health | v4 | 16.0 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-032 | hydraulic | v4 | 17.3 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-033 | quality | v4 | 18.6 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-034 | power | v4 | 16.8 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-035 | public-health | v4 | 18.1 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-036 | hydraulic | v4 | 16.3 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-037 | quality | v4 | 17.6 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-038 | power | v4 | 18.9 | open-findings | superseded |\n| RDY-039 | public-health | v4 | 17.1 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-040 | hydraulic | v4 | 18.4 | open-findings | current |\n| RDY-041 | quality | v4 | 16.6 | open-findings | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nList blockers, falsifiers, residual risks, owners, current evidence, and acceptance.\nKeep independent review separate from execution, communication, and closure authority.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"replace_evidence_ledger\",\"content\":\"# Solace Evidence and Decision Matrix\\n\\n| ID | Domain | Source | Fact/Observation | Unit/Value | Status | Dependencies | Conflicts/Unknowns | Candidate Currency | Citations |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| E-01 | Authority | AURORA | County health officer lifts do-not-drink only after current lab/distribution verification | n/a | Active | CIPHER, BASTION | Utility repair ≠ public-health authorization | W7 | [AURORA] |\\n| E-02 | Authority | AURORA | Final closure requires utility director acceptance of all blockers/risks | n/a | Active | NEXUS | Residual risk must be explicit | W7 | [AURORA] |\\n| E-03 | Hydraulic | BASTION | Min distribution pressure north zone | 42 psi | Current | DELTA, ECHO | Warning 38 psi vs Isolation 30 psi distinct | W7/H12 | [BASTION] |\\n| E-04 | Hydraulic | BASTION | Ridge storage volume / 12-hr emergency reserve | 5.8M gal / 3.2M gal | Current | DELTA | Gallons vs treated reserve distinct | W7/H12 | [BASTION] |\\n| E-05 | Sampling | CIPHER | Clearance requires two complete rounds ≥16 hours apart | n/a | Active | BASTION, GARNET | One clean round insufficient | W7 | [CIPHER] |\\n| E-06 | Sampling | CIPHER | Benzene reporting limit / action threshold | 0.5 µg/L / 5.0 µg/L | Current | GARNET | Reporting limit ≠ action threshold; µg/L not mg/L | W7 | [CIPHER] |\\n| E-07 | Pump | DELTA | Pump sequencing depends on BASTION pressure and ECHO power | n/a | Active | BASTION, ECHO | Cavitation constraints apply | W7/P9 | [DELTA] |\\n| E-08 | Power | ECHO | Emergency generation capacity/duration | 4.1 MW / 36 hrs | Current | KESTREL | Excludes mobile-pump load; not 36 days | W7 | [ECHO] |\\n| E-09 | Power | ECHO | Grid feed rated vs usable power | 8.2 MW rated / 6.5 MW usable | Current | DELTA | Damaged switchgear limits delivery | W7 | [ECHO] |\\n| E-10 | Treatment | FALCON | Free chlorine entry vs distribution thresholds | 0.8–2.0 mg/L entry / ≥0.2 mg/L dist | Current | INDIGO | Entry and distribution controls distinct; mg/L not µg/L | W7/T6 | [FALCON] |\\n| E-11 | Treatment | FALCON | Combined-filter turbidity current vs release gate | 0.18 NTU / ≤0.30 NTU (4 hrs) | Current | INDIGO | 0.18 NTU is not chlorine residual | W7/T6 | [FALCON] |\\n| E-12 | Source | GARNET | Ash-plume intake impact probability next rain | 34% forecast | Active | CIPHER, FALCON | Forecast probability ≠ measured contamination; reservoir vs river intake distinct | W7 | [GARNET] |\\n| E-13 | Source | GARNET | Chemical yard investigation hold active | n/a | Active | CIPHER | Containment trench not inspected below grade | W7 | [GARNET] |\\n| E-14 | Access | HELIX | SCADA token revoked; controller key current (W4) | n/a | Current | INDIGO, MOSAIC | Break-glass expires 2 hrs + dual approval; emergency ≠ continuing auth | W7/W4 | [HELIX] |\\n| E-15 | Telemetry | INDIGO | Critical-signal coverage | 96% covered / 4% unobserved | Current | BASTION, DELTA, ECHO, FALCON | Coverage ≠ confidence; uninstrumented zones not proven healthy | W7 | [INDIGO] |\\n| E-16 | Telemetry | INDIGO | Pressure warning vs isolation trigger | 38 psi warn / 30 psi isolate | Current | BASTION | Warning and action thresholds must remain distinct | W7 | [INDIGO] |\\n| E-17 | Environmental | JASPER | Unauthorized discharge notice clock | 72 hours from determination | Active | GARNET, FALCON, LUMEN | Determination event ≠ detection time; AURORA owns materiality | W7 | [JASPER] |\\n| E-18 | Environmental | JASPER | Emergency dechlorination residual limit | ≤0.019 mg/L at outfall | Current | FALCON | Immediate stop required if exceeded; permit E-17 | W7 | [JASPER] |\\n| E-19 | Logistics | KESTREL | Diesel stock coverage emergency vs full pump load | 36 hrs / 22 hrs | Current | ECHO, DELTA | Load regimes distinct; not days | W7 | [KESTREL] |\\n| E-20 | Logistics | KESTREL | Coagulant/chlorine stock duration | 4.5 days / 3.2 days | Current | FALCON | Inventory duration ≠ delivery lead time | W7 | [KESTREL] |\\n| E-21 | Public | LUMEN | Do-not-drink notice delivery coverage | 91% registered endpoints | Current | CIPHER, AURORA | Missing 9% is comm uncertainty, not pop reduction | W7 | [LUMEN] |\\n| E-22 | Public | LUMEN | Call center capacity vs forecast demand | 3,200/hr (6 hrs) / 4,100/hr forecast | Current | KESTREL | Alternate-language outreach may reduce repeats | W7 | [LUMEN] |\\n| E-23 | Change | MOSAIC | Current recovery candidate | W7 (H12, P9, T6, W4) | Current | ALL | W6 evidence historical unless transferred/rechecked | W7 | [MOSAIC] |\\n| E-24 | Change | MOSAIC | Rollback to W6 mechanical possibility | Valve map V8 + firmware C11 compatible | Active | BASTION, CIPHER, DELTA, ECHO, FALCON, HELIX | Mechanical possibility ≠ authorization | W7→W6 | [MOSAIC] |\\n| E-25 | Readiness | NEXUS | Open findings count | 16 (5 hyd, 4 treat, 3 samp, 2 pow, 2 comm) | Current | ALL | Finding count ≠ readiness percentage | W7 | [NEXUS] |\\n| E-26 | Readiness | NEXUS | Blocking findings | Incomplete 2nd-round samples; stale gen transfer evidence; missing PH duty officer ack | Active | CIPHER, ECHO, AURORA | Independent review required; no self-authorization | W7 | [NEXUS] |\\n\\n## Cross-Source Dependencies\\n- CIPHER sampling consumes BASTION flow paths and GARNET hypotheses [CIPHER, BASTION, GARNET].\\n- DELTA pump sequencing depends on BASTION pressure and ECHO power [DELTA, BASTION, ECHO].\\n- FALCON treatment selection depends on GARNET source hypotheses [FALCON, GARNET].\\n- INDIGO telemetry supports BASTION, DELTA, ECHO, FALCON but each retains own decision gate [INDIGO, BASTION, DELTA, ECHO, FALCON].\\n- HELIX audit events consumed by INDIGO; HELIX does not authorize access [HELIX, INDIGO].\\n- JASPER environmental notices depend on GARNET source impact and FALCON discharge conditions [JASPER, GARNET, FALCON].\\n- KESTREL fuel supports ECHO generator duration; KESTREL chemicals support FALCON staging [KESTREL, ECHO, FALCON].\\n- LUMEN communications depend on CIPHER/AURORA advisory status and INDIGO/BASTION service observations [LUMEN, CIPHER, AURORA, INDIGO, BASTION].\\n- MOSAIC candidate changes make BASTION, CIPHER, DELTA, ECHO, FALCON, HELIX evidence stale [MOSAIC, BASTION, CIPHER, DELTA, ECHO, FALCON, HELIX].\\n- NEXUS consumes all sources for independent review but does not mutate states [NEXUS, ALL].\\n\\n## Conflicts and Unknowns\\n- GARNET ash-plume 34% is forecast, not observed contamination; reservoir (non-detect) vs river intake (3.1 µg/L) must not be merged [GARNET].\\n- Chemical yard investigation hold active; trench inspection below grade pending [GARNET].\\n- INDIGO 4% unobserved coverage does not prove healthy uninstrumented zones [INDIGO].\\n- HELIX break-glass access expired; remote automation restoration requires named evidence [HELIX].\\n- NEXUS blocking findings: second-round samples incomplete, generator transfer evidence stale, PH duty officer acknowledgment missing [NEXUS].\\n\\n## Candidate Currency\\nCurrent candidate W7 (H12, P9, T6, W4) [MOSAIC]. Any mutation to hydraulic model, pump plan, treatment plan, key set, valve map, or firmware makes prior evidence stale and requires recheck [MOSAIC]. Rollback to W6 mechanically possible only with V8/C11 compatibility but not authorized [MOSAIC].\\n\\n## Falsifiers for Important Claims\\n- If CIPHER second-round samples show benzene ≥5.0 µg/L at any location, clearance claim falsified [CIPHER].\\n- If ECHO generator transfer evidence remains stale after recheck, 36-hr duration claim falsified [ECHO].\\n- If AURORA public-health duty officer does not acknowledge, closure claim falsified [AURORA].\\n- If FALCON turbidity exceeds 0.30 NTU for >4 hrs, release gate claim falsified [FALCON].\\n- If INDIGO coverage drops below 96% or unobserved zones show adverse conditions, telemetry adequacy claim falsified [INDIGO].\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"candidate:EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md\",\"object_version\":\"candidate-v001:370e9686a9df334cd023b92f114ac6b50a9ec54f44527b3b0380cfe6817ed310\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-008\",\"result_kind\":\"candidate_effect\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"after_sha256\":\"370e9686a9df334cd023b92f114ac6b50a9ec54f44527b3b0380cfe6817ed310\",\"before_sha256\":\"9a228857dd50e69921af6d67c22e74bd3156dfb6266475ce63838881a822da61\",\"candidate_version\":\"candidate-v001:370e9686a9df334cd023b92f114ac6b50a9ec54f44527b3b0380cfe6817ed310\",\"cause\":\"actor_replace_evidence_ledger\",\"changed_file\":\"EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md\",\"current_candidate_verification_status\":\"not_run_after_candidate_effect\",\"prior_check_bi