y externalized source ID>\nSOURCE_VERSION: <exact 64-hex version>\nEVIDENCE_RESULT: <exact newly externalized RESULT ID>\nEVIDENCE_ANCHOR: <one exact unique single-line substring copied from that source inside the delivered result>\nMODE: source_reported_fact or source_reported_relationship\nATTRIBUTION: owner_source_reported\nREFERENTS: NONE or comma-separated exact source IDs named by both the statement and the anchor's containing source line\nAUTHORITY: non_authoritative_derivative\nSTATEMENT: <one complete single-line source-attributed fact or relationship>\n\nThe host, not you, resolves the exact anchor, derives its containing complete source line, byte offsets, hashes, source/version binding, and reopen path. Copy only the smallest exact substring that supports the statement. The containing line preserves adjacent context and qualifications. Each claim is admitted independently; rejected claims consume cost and are discarded without repair or retry. A zero-valid update leaves prior state unchanged and ordinary task work continues.\n\nEmit at most 4 claims per source and 8 total, <= 1500 tokenizer tokens overall and <= 650 per source. A fact cannot name an external source. A relationship may name external objects when the owner-source context names them, but cannot mutate their slots or assert their authoritative current state. Cross-source synthesis belongs in exact task work, not this register.\n\nNEW SOURCE VERSIONS\nKESTREL: 2536c9c9d966266ccfecd69690d7575dcb4025b53ab52812cece766b0077c600\nLUMEN: 1a50bae39974b3c33c2a0a6b6b94859b75f41e3c4d4a01f17cf519db7b98253c\n\nPRIOR CURRENT RECORDS FOR THESE SOURCES\n# Anchored provenance-local source register\n\nEMPTY\n\n\nAUTHORITATIVE TASK (relevance only; never evidence)\n# Authoritative task — Solace regional-water recovery decision\n\nSolace County must restore a regional drinking-water network after wildfire,\npower, treatment, hydraulic, and control-system disturbances. Build and maintain\nthe exact candidate files, then propose submission only when the package is\ngenuinely ready for independent review.\n\nThe world contains fourteen exact, versioned source objects with opaque IDs.\nCatalog titles help navigation but do not supply findings. Read the bytes needed\nfor the work and cite sources as `[SOURCE_ID]`.\n\n## Required exact work\n\nMaintain `EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md` as a compact task-native evidence and\ndecision matrix. Preserve source-bound facts, cross-source dependencies,\nconflicts, unknowns, candidate currency, and citations. This exact artifact is\nnon-authoritative but may carry cumulative work across context turnover.\n\nConstruct `BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md` as a 1,500–2,100-word Solace\nWater Recovery Decision with exactly the declared section headings. Use at\nleast eleven distinct source IDs and integrate—not merely list—the governing\nrelationships.\n\nAddress all twelve requirement groups:\n\n- Q01 — incident, utility, public-health, communication, and closure authority;\n- Q02 — pressure, storage, isolation, residence time, and candidate-bound hydraulics;\n- Q03 — sampling rounds, spacing, detection limits, action thresholds, and staleness;\n- Q04 — pump capacity, shared-main limits, staged demand, and current evidence;\n- Q05 — grid, generator, fuel, staffing, chemicals, and resource contingencies;\n- Q06 — treatment barriers, turbidity, disinfectant, source blend, and contact time;\n- Q07 — contamination hypotheses, observations, locations, investigation holds, and falsifiers;\n- Q08 — access, token and key state, immutable custody, retention, and automation restoration;\n- Q09 — telemetry coverage, warnings versus actions, delays, alternates, and uncertainty;\n- Q10 — environmental determination, notice clock, permits, discharge, and evidence custody;\n- Q11 — public advisories, accessibility, alternate water, service states, and communications;\n- Q12 — candidate lineage, rollback, effect uptake, current checks, blockers, independent readiness, and closure.\n\n## Relationship rules\n\nPreserve psi versus kPa, gallons versus treated reserve, micrograms versus\nmilligrams, reporting limits versus action thresholds, percentages versus\nmeasured concentration, rated versus usable power, nameplate versus shared\ncapacity, warnings versus isolation triggers, forecast versus observation, and\nmechanical checks versus public-health and independent readiness. Candidate,\nhydraulic, sampling, treatment, pump, power, key, role, telemetry, or source-\nwater changes can make earlier evidence stale.\n\nThe decision must state owners, inputs, resources, timing, dependencies,\neffects, observations, contingencies, rollback and retirement conditions, and\nevidence that would falsify important claims. Do not infer that a provenance\nrecord, mutation, green check, or submission establishes readiness.\n\n\nEXACT NEWLY EXTERNALIZED RESULTS\n--- NEWLY EXTERNALIZED RESULT-006 ---\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:KESTREL:1-64+LUMEN:1-64\",\"object_version\":\"acd9bcd350f165ef046fccf06217402b1be7412e46e2312f76c416539a3bb8b8\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-006\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"KESTREL\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"LUMEN\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":7854}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"KESTREL\",\"source_path\":\"sources/KESTREL_LOGISTICS.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"2536c9c9d966266ccfecd69690d7575dcb4025b53ab52812cece766b0077c600\",\"source_size_bytes\":3584,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Fuel, chemicals, staffing, and mutual-aid logistics\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nCurrent diesel stock covers thirty-six hours at emergency load and twenty-two hours at full pump load. The two consumption regimes must remain distinct.\nCoagulant stock covers 4.5 days at the current source blend, while chlorine covers 3.2 days. Inventory duration is not delivery lead time.\nMutual aid provides six certified operators beginning at 06:00 UTC; travel uncertainty is plus or minus ninety minutes.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nECHO generator duration depends on KESTREL fuel; FALCON treatment staging depends on chemical stock; DELTA depends on certified staffing.\nLUMEN publishes public tanker locations only after AURORA and HELIX approve safety and access controls.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| LOG-000 | diesel | v2 | 36.0 | hours-cover | superseded |\n| LOG-001 | chlorine | v2 | 37.3 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-002 | operators | v2 | 38.6 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-003 | mobile-tankers | v2 | 36.8 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-004 | diesel | v2 | 38.1 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-005 | chlorine | v2 | 36.3 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-006 | operators | v2 | 37.6 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-007 | mobile-tankers | v2 | 38.9 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-008 | diesel | v2 | 37.1 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-009 | chlorine | v2 | 38.4 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-010 | operators | v2 | 36.6 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-011 | mobile-tankers | v2 | 37.9 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-012 | diesel | v2 | 36.1 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-013 | chlorine | v2 | 37.4 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-014 | operators | v3 | 38.7 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-015 | mobile-tankers | v3 | 36.9 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-016 | diesel | v3 | 38.2 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-017 | chlorine | v3 | 36.4 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-018 | operators | v3 | 37.7 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-019 | mobile-tankers | v3 | 39.0 | hours-cover | superseded |\n| LOG-020 | diesel | v3 | 37.2 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-021 | chlorine | v3 | 38.5 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-022 | operators | v3 | 36.7 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-023 | mobile-tankers | v3 | 38.0 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-024 | diesel | v3 | 36.2 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-025 | chlorine | v3 | 37.5 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-026 | operators | v3 | 38.8 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-027 | mobile-tankers | v3 | 37.0 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-028 | diesel | v4 | 38.3 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-029 | chlorine | v4 | 36.5 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-030 | operators | v4 | 37.8 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-031 | mobile-tankers | v4 | 36.0 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-032 | diesel | v4 | 37.3 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-033 | chlorine | v4 | 38.6 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-034 | operators | v4 | 36.8 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-035 | mobile-tankers | v4 | 38.1 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-036 | diesel | v4 | 36.3 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-037 | chlorine | v4 | 37.6 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-038 | operators | v4 | 38.9 | hours-cover | superseded |\n| LOG-039 | mobile-tankers | v4 | 37.1 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-040 | diesel | v4 | 38.4 | hours-cover | current |\n| LOG-041 | chlorine | v4 | 36.6 | hours-cover | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nPreserve load regime, stock type, days versus hours, staffing time, and uncertainty.\nName reorder triggers, alternates, owner, and retirement evidence.\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"LUMEN\",\"source_path\":\"sources/LUMEN_PUBLIC.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"1a50bae39974b3c33c2a0a6b6b94859b75f41e3c4d4a01f17cf519db7b98253c\",\"source_size_bytes\":3813,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Public warnings, accessibility, and customer continuity\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nDo-not-drink notices reached 91 percent of registered endpoints; the missing nine percent is communication uncertainty, not a nine-percent reduction in affected population.\nPublic states must distinguish do-not-use, do-not-drink, boil-water, restricted service, and cleared. Low pressure does not by itself establish contamination.\nThe call center can sustain 3,200 contacts per hour for six hours. Forecast demand is 4,100 per hour unless alternate-language outreach reduces repeat calls.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nCIPHER and AURORA determine advisory status; INDIGO and BASTION supply service observations. HELIX constrains publication of sensitive infrastructure details.\nJASPER supplies mandatory environmental language and KESTREL supplies verified alternate-water locations.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| COM-000 | sms | v2 | 91.0 | percent-delivered | superseded |\n| COM-001 | radio | v2 | 92.3 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-002 | clinics | v2 | 93.6 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-003 | schools | v2 | 91.8 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-004 | sms | v2 | 93.1 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-005 | radio | v2 | 91.3 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-006 | clinics | v2 | 92.6 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-007 | schools | v2 | 93.9 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-008 | sms | v2 | 92.1 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-009 | radio | v2 | 93.4 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-010 | clinics | v2 | 91.6 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-011 | schools | v2 | 92.9 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-012 | sms | v2 | 91.1 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-013 | radio | v2 | 92.4 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-014 | clinics | v3 | 93.7 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-015 | schools | v3 | 91.9 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-016 | sms | v3 | 93.2 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-017 | radio | v3 | 91.4 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-018 | clinics | v3 | 92.7 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-019 | schools | v3 | 94.0 | percent-delivered | superseded |\n| COM-020 | sms | v3 | 92.2 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-021 | radio | v3 | 93.5 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-022 | clinics | v3 | 91.7 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-023 | schools | v3 | 93.0 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-024 | sms | v3 | 91.2 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-025 | radio | v3 | 92.5 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-026 | clinics | v3 | 93.8 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-027 | schools | v3 | 92.0 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-028 | sms | v4 | 93.3 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-029 | radio | v4 | 91.5 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-030 | clinics | v4 | 92.8 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-031 | schools | v4 | 91.0 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-032 | sms | v4 | 92.3 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-033 | radio | v4 | 93.6 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-034 | clinics | v4 | 91.8 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-035 | schools | v4 | 93.1 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-036 | sms | v4 | 91.3 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-037 | radio | v4 | 92.6 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-038 | clinics | v4 | 93.9 | percent-delivered | superseded |\n| COM-039 | schools | v4 | 92.1 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-040 | sms | v4 | 93.4 | percent-delivered | current |\n| COM-041 | radio | v4 | 91.6 | percent-delivered | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nPreserve delivery coverage, state vocabulary, capacity, forecast, accessibility, and privacy.\nState owners, channels, timing, acknowledgments, alternates, and retirement evidence.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n","generated":""}
